diff --git a/src/testing/fuzzing/syzkaller/README.md b/src/testing/fuzzing/syzkaller/README.md
index 56a1627c3c5..fdf0c0e6780 100644
--- a/src/testing/fuzzing/syzkaller/README.md
+++ b/src/testing/fuzzing/syzkaller/README.md
@@ -1,9 +1,67 @@
 This directory contains definitions needed to build and run
 [syzkaller](https://github.com/google/syzkaller) against Fuchsia's system call
-interfaces.
+interfaces with kernel sanitizer coverage.
 
-- The top-level directory is relevant for Zircon fuzzing (currently on pause:
-  https://fxbug.dev/296220035). Its BUILD.gn contains rules to build syzkaller's
-  `syz-executor` component for Fuchsia.
+- The top-level directory is relevant for Zircon fuzzing. Its BUILD.gn contains
+  rules to build syzkaller's `syz-executor` component for Fuchsia.
 
 - The `starnix` subdirectory is relevant for Starnix fuzzing (currently active).
+
+## Build
+
+Use a kernel sancov variant and include this package:
+
+```sh
+fx set core.x64 \
+  --variant=sancov \
+  --with //src/testing/fuzzing/syzkaller \
+  --with-base //bundles/tools
+fx build //src/testing/fuzzing/syzkaller
+```
+
+The build produces the target-side `syz-executor-pkg` package. Build the
+host-side syzkaller tools from the syzkaller checkout with:
+
+```sh
+cd third_party/syzkaller
+make TARGETOS=fuchsia TARGETARCH=amd64 TARGETVMARCH=amd64 manager execprog
+```
+
+## Run
+
+Start and package a Fuchsia image with `syz-executor-pkg` available, then use a
+manager config similar to:
+
+```json
+{
+  "name": "fuchsia-zircon",
+  "target": "fuchsia/amd64",
+  "http": "127.0.0.1:56741",
+  "workdir": "/tmp/syzkaller-fuchsia",
+  "kernel_obj": "$FUCHSIA_DIR/out/default/zircon.elf",
+  "kernel_src": "$FUCHSIA_DIR",
+  "syzkaller": "$FUCHSIA_DIR/third_party/syzkaller",
+  "procs": 4,
+  "cover": true,
+  "sandbox": "none",
+  "type": "qemu",
+  "vm": {
+    "count": 1,
+    "kernel": "$FUCHSIA_DIR/out/default/multiboot.bin",
+    "initrd": "$FUCHSIA_DIR/out/default/fuchsia.zbi",
+    "cpu": 4,
+    "mem": 4096,
+    "qemu_args": "-nographic"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Then run:
+
+```sh
+third_party/syzkaller/bin/syz-manager -config /path/to/fuchsia.cfg
+```
+
+`syz-executor` runs in the target as the RPC runner. When coverage is enabled, it
+maps the kernel `sancov` and `sancov-counts` debugdata VMOs and reports newly hit
+PCs back to syzkaller so corpus mutation is coverage guided.
